From 22f0ccb7052fa4b05299807cfa4d3d64d4511f87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:24:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] arming: refuse to arm into a mode that would itself start
 a manoeuvre

canArm() had no mode check. USER_1..4 select STUNT/PATTERN while
disarmed, and stunt::start/pattern::start run at mode entry regardless of
the arm state, so a yaw spin queued on the bench fired at full rate the
instant the vehicle armed. USER_5 / ATUNE=1 latch autotune_active while
disarmed with the same effect, and AUTOTUNE / MOTOR_TUNE / MOTOR_DETECT
were "select, then arm to start".

canArm() now refuses, before and independent of ARMING_CHECK (which skips
sensor checks on a bench, not this), while the mode is STUNT, PATTERN,
AUTOTUNE, MOTOR_TUNE or MOTOR_DETECT, or an autotune is pending, with a
reason that says what to do ("PreArm: STUNT queued - select a flight
mode", "... - arm first, then select", "autotune pending - set ATUNE=0";
all fit STATUSTEXT). The workflow is now uniformly: arm in a flight mode,
then select the manoeuvre.

So a pending trigger is not a dead end, ATUNE=0 now withdraws it while
disarmed (previously only arming - which starts the tune - cleared it).
The MOTOR_TUNE OLED hint changes to "MTune: arm, then select".

The joystick-button arm path does not go through canArm and is untouched
(tracked upstream as issue #6).

Companion: mongla_ws's autotune/motor_tune already arm first and then set
the mode, so they are unaffected. ARCHITECTURE.md and PARAMETERS.md
updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KchLnXUAMJ6S4pj3BZLobN
